  Avoid leaving deletion half-committed when secret cleanup fails.

  The server definition is already deleted when deleteOwnedMCPSecrets
  runs. A failure—or request cancellation—returns an error but leaves
  orphaned secrets, and retrying the deletion now returns not found. Persist
  an idempotent cleanup intent before deletion, retry cleanup durably, or
  provide full rollback semantics.


