  internal/settings/mcp_catalog_install.go:62-84 — Avoid reloading MCP state
  after the write succeeds
  installedMCPItemWithoutProbe re-reads all MCP sources, so an unrelated
  malformed source file can make InstallMCPCatalog return an error even
  though the new server is already persisted and the install notification
  never fires. Build the returned item from the committed write instead of
  depending on a second catalog load.


